<title>NORWAY: Coca-Cola extends Norway distribution agreement.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola extends Norway distribution agreement.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian food-based conglomerate Orkla ASA said on Friday The Coca-Cola Company (TCCC) had extended a distribution agreement in Norway by two months until May 1, 1997.</p>
<p>TCCC had agreed the distribution contract with brewing company Pripps-Ringnes, a joint venture between Orkla and Swedish car maker Volvo.</p>
<p>Orkla said the extension was in accordance with an earlier letter of intent giving TCCC the option to continue distribution in Norway for three months from March 1, 1997.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
